# M15 "Repository": what a folder offers depends on the marker its own tool left in it, and on
# what the selection can carry. The folders here are marker fixtures — an empty `.git`, `.hg`,
# `.svn`, `CVS/Repository` or `vssver2.scc` is all the marker a tool leaves, and detection reads
# nothing else; what the clients themselves answer is pinned by the scenarios of src/repo.

# A folder Git owns: the working copy's commands are there, and Clone is not — a folder the tool
# already owns has nothing to clone into.
open $T/gitcopy
expect-menu-item Commit
expect-menu-item Pull
expect-menu-item Sync
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-menu-item Show Log
expect-menu-item Browse Repository
expect-menu-item Settings
expect-no-menu-item Clone…

# A plain folder: the Repository entry is still there, and its submenu carries only Clone.
open $T/plain
expect-menu-item Repository
expect-menu-item Clone…
expect-no-menu-item Commit
expect-no-menu-item Push

# A CVS folder is a central store: nothing local to send out, nothing of one's own to stash.
open $T/cvs
expect-menu-item Pull
expect-menu-item Commit
expect-no-menu-item Push
expect-no-menu-item Sync
expect-no-menu-item Stash
expect-no-menu-item Clone…

# Mercurial has both a stash of its own and something to push.
open $T/hgcopy
expect-menu-item Stash
expect-menu-item Push
expect-no-menu-item Clone…

# A Subversion working copy reads its settings from the folder's properties.
open $T/svncopy
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-menu-item Settings
expect-no-menu-item Stash

# A Visual Source Safe binding answers Blame with nothing, renames nothing through its own client,
# and keeps a local copy of what it deletes.
open $T/vsscopy
select a.txt
expect-menu-item Delete (keep local)
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-no-menu-item Blame
expect-no-menu-item Rename
expect-no-menu-item Settings
expect-no-menu-item Clone…

# A folder that only holds a working copy deeper down is not one itself: Clone stays.
open $T/wrapper
expect-menu-item Clone…
expect-no-menu-item Commit

# and the folder the marker sits in is the working copy.
open $T/wrapper/inner
expect-menu-item Commit
expect-no-menu-item Clone…

# One file can be compared with its previous version, renamed, blamed and deleted; two cannot be
# renamed as one thing.
open $T/gitcopy
select one.txt
expect-menu-item Diff with previous version
expect-menu-item Rename
expect-menu-item Blame
expect-menu-item Delete and add to ignore list

open $T/gitcopy
select one.txt | two.txt
expect-no-menu-item Rename
expect-no-menu-item Diff with previous version
expect-menu-item Delete

# Nothing selected: the folder's own diff and history remain, the per-item commands do not.
open $T/gitcopy
select-none
expect-menu-item Diff
expect-menu-item Check for modifications
expect-no-menu-item Rename
expect-no-menu-item Blame

# A folder inside a working copy reached from a parent marker is one too, and the marker of a
# sibling folder does not reach across.
open $T/gitcopy/deep
expect-menu-item Commit
expect-menu-item Switch/Checkout…
